Command               	Purpose
ls	            List files and directories
cd	            Change the current directory
pwd           	Print the current working directory
cat           	Display or combine file contents
echo	          Print text or variables
man	            Display a command's manual page
history	        Show previously executed commands
clear	          Clear the terminal screen

ls — List Directory Contents...Displays the files and folders in the current directory.
Syntax: ls [options] [directory]
 Flag     Description              
-l       Long listing format (permissions, owner, size, date) 
-a   Show hidden files (those beginning with `.`)         
-h   Human-readable file sizes (used with `-l`)           
-R   Recursively list subdirectories                      
-t   Sort by modification time                            
-S   Sort by file size                                    

cd — Change Directory....Moves between directories.
Syntax: cd directory
Command    	Meaning
cd	      Go to home directory
cd ..   	Move up one directory
cd -    	Return to previous directory
cd ~    	Go to home directory
cd /    	Go to filesystem root

pwd — Print Working Directory....Displays the full path of your current location.
Syntax: pwd
Flag  	 Description
-P	   Show the physical path (resolve symbolic links)
